  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The model's performance and scalability were only demonstrated on two simplified test cases rather than a real-world metropolitan network.",
      "what": "This study reviews multimodal transportation models incorporating shared mobility services and introduces a new multimodal traffic assignment model formulated as a Mixed-Integer Bilinear Programming problem. The model accommodates both continuous and integer settings, allowing commuters to combine public transit and shared mobility to optimize travel time and monetary costs. The framework was evaluated using two test cases to analyze user mode and path choices alongside the price of anarchy.",
      "why": "It provides a mathematical framework that explicitly captures the synergies and combinations between public transit and shared mobility services, correcting a common gap in traffic assignment models that treat these systems in isolation."
    }
